  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The Graph Edge Attention Network (GREAT) optimizes electric vehicle routing and charging by operating entirely on edge-based energy metrics rather than Euclidean node coordinates. Trained within an end-to-end reinforcement learning framework using San Francisco road topology and physical energy consumption data, the model was evaluated across San Francisco, Vienna, and Gothenburg using battery capacities from 15 to 40 kWh. GREAT achieved up to an 8.78% energy reduction compared to a strong heuristic while running 60 times faster, and provided effective initializations for adaptive large neighborhood search algorithms.",
      "why": "The model replaces traditional node-based neural solvers with an edge-centric architecture, enabling machine learning routing methods to natively handle asymmetric physical energy costs caused by real-world terrain and road networks."
    }
  },
